    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are `AcceptanceBase` and likely a support file. The full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I changed to satisfy the spec:\n\n**Behavior:** When creating an owner via `POST /api/owners` that is *not* a hard identity duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id. Otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is `false`.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields, `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32), to the `Owner` schema. These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` fields.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 After the existing hard-duplicate (409) check and before saving, computes the soft match via a new `findPossibleDuplicate(...)` helper (matches on case-insensitive last name + equal postcode + different telephone; requires a postcode; picks the lowest id when several match for determinism), and stores the flag and matched id on the owner.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` auto-maps the two same-named fields from `Owner` to `OwnerDto`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns them. Tests: `AcceptanceTest` passes and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
